["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"entity-runtime","stream_identity":"01a0cab7-1ed7-77a5-8384-ff10c92e7ad6","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG3daf1a0d0ad8bc92604188fc16386146e5f3559ebbbfbd130b49709263323617","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/verifiable-decision-replay","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nEvent-only replay accepts unknown event types, cannot represent zero or multiple events per decision, and bypasses the rules that produced state.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA stored decision record can be rerun deterministically against its recorded definition snapshot, and any altered command, transition, field change or event is refused without producing state.\n\n## Implementation evidence\n\nMoved to implemented on 2026-09-09 after an audit of every non-implemented artifact against `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/roadmap.md` and the crates.\n\n`entity_core::replay` reruns each recorded command against its definition snapshot and refuses an altered command, transition, fields or events (`crates/entity-core/src/replay.rs`); `rehydrate` was hardened further for 0.18.0 (`docs/design/kernel-v0.1.md` § 10.1).\n","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:the-store-an-adopter-runs-on"},{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"History records enough normalized input and definition data to rerun decisions without trusting forged events.","title":"Replay verifies durable decision records"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG3daf1a0d0ad8bc92604188fc16386146e5f3559ebbbfbd130b49709263323617","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG3daf1a0d0ad8bc92604188fc16386146e5f3559ebbbfbd130b49709263323617"]}]